course: dictionary
lesson: 15933
title: Unremedied: not yet put right
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal, so you will meet them in news, law and reports more than in chatting with friends. Unremedied is one of them. Break it into parts: «un-» means not, and «remedied» means put right or fixed. So unremedied means not put right yet.
explain: «The broken swing stayed unremedied for a whole year.» The swing was still broken for a year because nobody had fixed it. Try the everyday swap: «not fixed». The sentence still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: In everyday talk, say «not fixed» or «not sorted». Keep unremedied for writing and reading, and you will see it in reports about wrongs and unfairness. An unremedied wrong is one that still has not been put right.
fact: Unremedied means not put right, cured or fixed.
fact: The prefix un- means not, as in unhappy and unsafe.
fact: «The leak stayed unremedied all winter» means nobody fixed the leak.
fact: In everyday talk, use «not fixed» or «not sorted» instead.
fact: An unremedied wrong is one that has not yet been made right, so people may still ask for justice.
exercise: «The pothole stayed unremedied for six months.» What does unremedied mean here? | *Not yet fixed | Filled with water | Very deep and dangerous | Made bigger on purpose
exercise: Which plain words could replace unremedied in everyday talk? | sorted out | painted bright | *not sorted | finished at last
exercise: Break unremedied into parts. What does un- mean? | before | very | *not | again
test: «The unfair rule remained unremedied for years.» What does unremedied mean? | Very kind | *Not yet put right | Put right twice | Hidden from view
test: Which sentence uses unremedied correctly? | The unremedied sun was bright | The children unremedied their lunch quickly | *The unremedied wrong still needs to be put right | The unremedied dog ran home
exam: In a news report, an unremedied injustice means what? | A fair law that everyone follows | A small mistake that nobody noticed | *An injustice that has still not been put right | An injustice that has been put right
